      "message": "An absolute path makes all three members share one cache directory, unlike every other suite here, where a relative name resolves under each member\u0027s own cache/. yangtools writes entries with a plain Files.copy onto the target file, guarded only by Files.exists, so two members writing the same model could leave one reading a truncated .yang. Am I right that nothing stops that?",
