      "writtenOn": "2026-08-27T07:48:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "responding to comment 1 (this one), 5 and 7, since all three come down to the absolute path, so they\u0027re fixed together: \n\nthe directory is now the relative name bug8086-schema. DefaultSchemaResourceManager resolves the configured name against \"cache\" via Path.resolve, which returns the argument unchanged when it\u0027s absolute.. so /tmp/schema did exactly what you said, while a relative name lands under each member\u0027s own cache. After a run:\n```tests/opendaylight-member-{1,2,3}/cache/bug8086-schema/``` - one per member\nNetconf connector for device netconf-test-device will use schema cache directory bug8086-schema instead of schema.\nSo the three members no longer share a directory (no concurrent writes of the same file), the value is load-bearing rather than equal to the library default, and nothing lives in /tmp, which also removes the rm -rf of a path this suite doesn\u0027t own. The directories sit inside the member distributions that staging recreates each run, so there\u0027s no cleanup step at all now. Each member\u0027s cache also accumulates the models it fetched from the device, which is further proof it\u0027s per-member.",
      "parentUuid": "62fb962b_16527ae3",
      "revId": "ebccbc89ffc35e59168ed70887944fc98647aeee",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
